      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140411_18071285_0001.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140411_18071285_0001&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140411_18071285_0001.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140411_18061181_0002.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140411_18061181_0002&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140411_18061181_0002.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Liam, To: Elijah H. Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Postcard Info: Co-Mo Foto Co., Watertown, Wis.&lt;br&gt;
Picture Info: Main Street East Dunlap IA. 08250&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Dunlap, Iowa on June 5, 1921&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mr. Elijah H. Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;6/4 Sat.&lt;br&gt;
Got here about 7 pm. Had a good trip in two days, and everybody O.K. Just drove 8 hours to Crepo looking for girls. Will write soon.&lt;br&gt;
Hello to all,&lt;br&gt;
Liam&lt;br&gt;
Mrs. Rush mentioned that she is getting along O.K.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
